GET /v1/chats/{id}/messages | messages | Either member reads chronological history when enabled, otherwise only the latest chat message. after is an exclusive message-sequence cursor. Repeate
POST /v1/chats/{id}/messages | send | Send exact UTF-8 as the authenticated participant. Prohibited communication is delivered and flagged. A retry reuses the original message and send aud
GET /v1/docs | docs | 
GET /v1/episodes/{id} | episode | 
GET /v1/episodes/{id}/balances | balances | 
POST /v1/episodes/{id}/challenges | challenge | 
GET /v1/episodes/{id}/chats | list | List only the caller's chats; the operator sees all episode chats. IDs form an opaque stable lexicographic cursor. Listing is audited.
POST /v1/episodes/{id}/chats | create | Create an immutable two-participant chat. Participants must include themselves and cannot set communication_prohibited=false. The operator may provisi
POST /v1/episodes/{id}/claims | claim | 
POST /v1/episodes/{id}/commitments | commitment | Selected juror commits a verdict and assessment and deposits the juror bond. The server generates and persists the secret salt; it is never returned.
GET /v1/episodes/{id}/forum/messages | get_forum_messages | Assigned participants read full chronological forum history. Every read is audited with exact returned sequence numbers. Operators use the separate tr
POST /v1/episodes/{id}/forum/messages | send_forum_message | Append exact UTF-8 to the episode-wide forum as the authenticated assigned participant. round_num is an optional caller-supplied annotation. Retried r
POST /v1/episodes/{id}/reveals | reveal | The same juror reveals previously persisted material during the chain-derived reveal window.
GET /v1/episodes/{id}/settlement | settlement | 
POST /v1/episodes/{id}/withdrawals | withdraw | Withdraw only the authenticated participant's entire global credit, which may contain entitlements from multiple episodes.
GET /v1/health | health | 
GET /v1/openapi.json | openapi_document | 
GET /v1/operations/{id} | operation | 
GET /v1/participants | participants | 
